iversities'' Foundation Program (WAUFP) <ul> <li>78</li> </ul> Western Australian Certificate of Education (WACE) 2016 onwards <ul> <li>96</li> </ul> <p> <a href="#8919493e-2843-49fc-9b37-63e04d50d377">View full details</a> </p> <!-- RichTextCourseCard.cshtml --> Admission requirements <p> For applicants with recent secondary education, information on admission criteria is available on our <a href="/study/how-to-apply/entry-requirements">entry requirements</a> page or on the <a href="https://handbooks.uwa.edu.au/">UWA Handbook</a> for course specific requirements and prerequisites.<br/> </p> Admission requirements <!-- RichTextCourseCard.cshtml --> ADMISSION REQUIREMENT English competency <p>English is the language of instruction and assessment at UWA and you will need to meet the <a href="https://www.uwa.edu.au/study/how-to-apply/english-language-requirements">English language requirements</a> of the University to be eligible for a place.</p> <p>Minimum overall IELTS score of 6.5, with no band less than 6.0.</p> ADMISSION REQUIREMENT English competency',
