    course_description = '<p>Environmental Science assesses the impact of human activity on the global environment and develops scientific, risk-based solutions to help secure a sustainable future. Environmental scientists deal with issues such as climate change, carbon trading, greenhouse gas emissions and habitat destruction. </p> <p>As a student of the Environmental Science and Management extended major, you will be trained to apply scientific, economic and regulatory knowledge to help society resolve these conflicts. The extended major further allows the shortest possible pathway into all specialisations in Environmental Science Master''s program at UWA excepting Marine and Coastal Processes.</p>',
